{"name":"Gull","hex":"#918c8f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Gull","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A player, supporter or other person connected with Torquay United Football Club."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Gull"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gull","blocks":[{"text":"Gulls, informally called seagulls, are seabirds of the subfamily Larinae. They are most closely related to terns and skimmers, and are placed with them in the family Laridae. They are also related, more distantly, to auks and skuas, and more distantly still to waders. Until the 21st century, most gulls were placed in the genus Larus, but that arrangement is now considered polyphyletic, leading to the readoption and revision of several genera."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Herring_Gull_%28Larus_argentatus%29%2C_Brighton%2C_England.JPG/330px-Herring_Gull_%28Larus_argentatus%29%2C_Brighton%2C_England.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gull","wikidata":"Q2699803"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Armenian_Gull_Juvenile_in_flight%2C_Sevan_lake.jpg/500px-Armenian_Gull_Juvenile_in_flight%2C_Sevan_lake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Armenian_Gull_Juvenile_in_flight%2C_Sevan_lake.jpg/1280px-Armenian_Gull_Juvenile_in_flight%2C_Sevan_lake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Armenian_Gull_Juvenile_in_flight%2C_Sevan_lake.jpg/500px-Armenian_Gull_Juvenile_in_flight%2C_Sevan_lake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Immature (probably 2nd year) Armenian gull in flight, flying over Lake Sevan","link":"htt